{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1206557-2e-true-pagan-multiple-tribes","id":1206557,"title":"[2E] \"True\" Pagan - Multiple Tribes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-13T12:01:03-07:00","id":1206557,"title":"[2E] \"True\" Pagan - Multiple Tribes","content":"I've got a character rattling around in my head based on a slew of influences. I'm having a hard time narrowing down a Tribe because both the Hunters in Darkness and Iron Masters seem to be really good fits. The biggest separator is Sacred Prey, but my group heavily underplays this facet of Tribes (largely due to this being a legacy game that made the edition jump midway through - we still have 1E Wolves running around and have narrative reasons for the mechanical changes.)<br /> <br /> Anyways, long story short,I was wondering what a Forsaken who followed two tribes would like. Would it be actually possible with mechanical tweaks? What would it look like in character? What would be the social ramifications? Et al.<br /> <br /> I was kind of imagining it like modern pagans, but Forsaken at large are already kind of like that - they recognize all the Firstborn, Luna, Urfarah, maybe even their pack totems. So how would it be different if they pledged to multiple Tribes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6310-twitchblues","name":"twitchblues","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T13:31:01-07:00","id":1206619,"title":"","content":"Probably lesser benefits all around. There's something similar as an option in the Blasphemies book among the Bale Hounds, where they can have a dark pantheon approach as opposed to a tribe or variety of lodges. A fitting way to do it in second edition without losing mechanical advantages would be something like being a member of A Tribe, while being a lodge member of one of B Tribe's pillars. For instance being a Storm Lord member of the Lodge of Garm (a pillar of the Blood Talons).<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, since every tribe can hunt any sacred prey, it's pretty easy to downplay it as a reason for joining a tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T15:04:05-07:00","id":1206674,"title":"","content":"Even true pagans had their castes dedicated to various factions of deityhood, from the service of specific gods in various cities in both Sumerian and Egyptian states to organizations such as the Vestal Virgins and the mystery religions of Greece. I could (really) go on.<br /> <br /> Tribes and lodges are like that-sure, these things are all viable and worthy of worship/practice-and-benefit in the name thereof, but there's a strong sense of those being chosen in the name of one in particular. The average &quot;pagan citizen&quot; would more likely be a Ghost Wolf. If someone wanted to work beneath two or more Tribes, it would more likely work out in something akin to how the Carthians infiltrate other Covenants than not-you start off with clout in one tribe, and then intermediary between two until you basically become a bridge between the two. Bonus points if you can start a Lodge explicitly for that purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-13-2018, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T16:13:15-07:00","id":1206709,"title":"","content":"I dont really know werewolf well so i might be mistaken but i thought tribes functioned (mechanically) like covenants in Requiem where you can be openly part of multiple covenants. Mechanically you can have the merit status(covenant) for as many covenant as you like so long as you dont exceed 5 points in total and your main covenant has the most point (i think) : Status (Carthians) ** and Status (Circle of the Crone) *.<br /> In the same vein can't you just have Status (Blood Talon) ** and Status (Iron Masters) *? Or is it prohibited in the game?<br /> <br /> Or am i just remembering everything (even the requiem stuff) wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T16:19:53-07:00","id":1206714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1206557-2e-true-pagan-multiple-tribes?p=1206709#post1206709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont really know werewolf well so i might be mistaken but i thought tribes functioned (mechanically) like covenants in Requiem where you can be openly part of multiple covenants. Mechanically you can have the merit status(covenant) for as many covenant as you like so long as you dont exceed 5 points in total and your main covenant has the most point (i think) : Status (Carthians) ** and Status (Circle of the Crone) *.<br /> In the same vein can't you just have Status (Blood Talon) ** and Status (Iron Masters) *? Or is it prohibited in the game?<br /> <br /> Or am i just remembering everything (even the requiem stuff) wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>With Requiem you can be a friend of another covenant, and sometimes get the benefits of it, but you can't really be like, an active Lancea et Sanctum and active Circle of the Crone member without considerable limitations. You can have Status in something, that doesn't necessarily mean you're a member, though. Honestly I suspect that was more because so many people complained about certain covenants having magic powers while others not, or that one covenant was 'objectively better' because of powers it brought to the table. Though it makes sense even without the mechanics considering the covenants are more social clubs than anything else.<br /> <br /> Tribes lean way more towards religions than the covenants do, easier more than the Lancea et Sanctum. And a clear sighted connection type, too, rather than relying on an (ironically) unseen ephemera. There's a spiritual bond one gets with their tribal totem, and even the nicest of tribal totems aren't likely to share.<br /> <br /> I think ArcaneArts had it right, if for some reason you wanted to be an 'equal' follower of all the tribal totems (or a bunch of them, at least) you would probably go ghost wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-13-2018, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T16:26:32-07:00","id":1206717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1206557-2e-true-pagan-multiple-tribes?p=1206714#post1206714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Requiem you can be a friend of another covenant, and sometimes get the benefits of it, but you can't really be like, a Lancea et Sanctum Circle of the Crone member. You can have Status in something, that doesn't necessarily mean you're a member, though.<br /> <br /> Tribes lean way more towards religions than the covenants do, easier more than the Lancea et Sanctum, and there's a spiritual bond one gets with their tribal totem, and even the nicest of tribal totems aren't likely to share.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well i think with a creative enough ST you could conjure up a workable way to be part of both the lancea and the circle. Tho i wouldn't put that situation as the norm.<br /> <br /> As for the tribes, i apologise for being like that sort of person, but i am wondering if there is anywhere in the book where its state that you cant be part of more than one tribe.<br /> Again, i'm not trying to make things difficult, I'm just curious if its a written rule. thx<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T16:44:38-07:00","id":1206725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1206557-2e-true-pagan-multiple-tribes?p=1206717#post1206717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the tribes, i apologise for being like that sort of person, but i am wondering if there is anywhere in the book where its state that you cant be part of more than one tribe.<br /> Again, i'm not trying to make things difficult, I'm just curious if its a written rule. thx</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, in character creation, under tribes. 'Characters belong to one of five tribes - or your character may be a ghost Wolf, without a tribe.' Every other mention of tribes also has it as personally singular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T17:30:28-07:00","id":1206738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1206557-2e-true-pagan-multiple-tribes?p=1206725#post1206725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, in character creation, under tribes. 'Characters belong to one of five tribes - or your character may be a ghost Wolf, without a tribe.' Every other mention of tribes also has it as personally singular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thx.<br /> I keep making the mistake of seeing the tribes as organisations (not unlike the vampires covenants and mages orders), whereas (like you said) they are more akin to religions or personal philosophies. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T18:01:16-07:00","id":1206744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>twitchblues</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1206557-2e-true-pagan-multiple-tribes#post1206557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was kind of imagining it like modern pagans, but Forsaken at large are already kind of like that - they recognize all the Firstborn, Luna, Urfarah, maybe even their pack totems. So how would it be different if they pledged to multiple Tribes?</div> </div> </div> </div>All werewolves are \u2018modern pagans\u2019 in this sense. Regardless of their personal philosophies, they recognize the Firstborn and all the other spirits because these things exist. They can follow the philosophies of multiple Firstborn as much as they want, but can\u2019t spiritually pledge themselves to more than one.<br /> <br /> The nature of totem bonds doesn\u2019t really allow multiple bonds at the same \u2018rung\u2019 of the spiritual hierarchy. Essentially, the half-spirit nature of every werewolf has a \u2018space\u2019 at each spiritual level*. This means a werewolf can have a pack totem at her weakest rung, but not two pack totems. She can have a lodge totem, but not two etc. The more powerful totem connects to a different \u2018space\u2019 in the werewolf\u2019s spirit, but once that bond is there, the werewolf can\u2019t have another bond of the same type. <br /> <br /> Even if this wasn\u2019t the case, a werewolf would have a very hard time of having two tribes, as the Firstborn are a powerful, prideful, squabbling lot, who don\u2019t tolerate dilution of their essence tithes to their siblings. Spirits are slaves to their natures, after all.<br /> <br /> As I see it, the tiers are roughly: Personal* - Pack* - Lodge - Tribe - Urfarah - Luna. <br /> <br /> * Pack totems and personal totems are a strange case. Though pack totems tend to be more powerful than personal totems, sometimes the reverse can occur and stil work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T00:45:25-07:00","id":1206808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1206557-2e-true-pagan-multiple-tribes?p=1206744#post1206744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see it, the tiers are roughly: Personal* - Pack* - Lodge - Tribe - Urfarah - Luna.<br /> <br /> * Pack totems and personal totems are a strange case. Though pack totems tend to be more powerful than personal totems, sometimes the reverse can occur and stil work.</div> </div> </div> </div>But can Uratha have one Firstborn as his Tribe Totem but then <i>other's</i> Firstborn brood spirit as his Personal Totem? Essentially, you are member of, for example, Red Wolf Church ( Iron Masters Tribe ) and have 'personal advisory' from the Winter Wolf's workers ( Storm Lords Tribe )?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T01:03:47-07:00","id":1206812,"title":"","content":"While interesting, I personally would rule it as a no. The Firstborn are prideful, selfish god-level spirits... the idea of pledging yourself to two or more is very, very risky and down right hubristic. It would only backfire; double dealing with any sufficiently powerful spirit is suicidally foolish, even if said spirits are nominally Allies like the Firstborn. Like Bunyip said, siblings they may be... but siblings fight- Especially over what they consider to be theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-14-2018, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:56:37-07:00","id":1206991,"title":"","content":"I mean, get that potential personal totem to pledge allegiance to the firstborn you follow and it should be fine. Also, I figure another restriction to a personal totem would be that it only counts your as it's spiritual children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T16:27:51-07:00","id":1207052,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of reasons to say no. Renown/Gift price breaks are something Order/Covenant Status don't buy in 2E, nor are the social groups equivalent, as Order and Covenant aren't caught up in prehistoric webs of pacts enforced by otherworldly beings. It's hard to imagine those spirits are going to casually divulge initiatory secrets to someone the murderous cannibal monsters it serves don't sign off on.<br /> <br /> Let's see. First Sagrim-Ur and Hikaon-Ur would first have to agree that sharing a werewolf is in both of their interests. Seems unlikely, but they require complementary vows, so it's not impossible. Red Wolf might be down for it, but I think Black Wolf likes her boundaries to be settled and ironclad. Furthermore, there are a lot of actions that can violate both vows simultaneously, so that's an immediate concern for any supplicant who wants to maintain Harmony. So, I think a trial that can meet both Firstborn's standards is the starting point.<br /> <br /> Benefits? I'm immediately put off by the potential for a third affinity Renown/Gift set. No fourth point of Renown or bonus Facet, right off the bat, but maybe a single Gift could be marked as an Affinity? I'd also limit any &quot;taught only to&quot; kind of Rites to be limited by dots in the auxiliary Tribe's Renown. The Sacred Hunt must be relearned as though it was a separate rite for each Tribe.<br /> <br /> That's where I'd start. I'm not really big on Tribes as anything much more than the means by which an Uratha joins the People, let alone initiating an individual twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T17:40:00-07:00","id":1207080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1206557-2e-true-pagan-multiple-tribes?p=1206808#post1206808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But can Uratha have one Firstborn as his Tribe Totem but then <i>other's</i> Firstborn brood spirit as his Personal Totem? Essentially, you are member of, for example, Red Wolf Church ( Iron Masters Tribe ) and have 'personal advisory' from the Winter Wolf's workers ( Storm Lords Tribe )?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but depending on what you mean by \u2018Firstborn brood spirit\u2019 you may have additional difficulties. <br /> <br /> If you mean a small spirit who comes from the Firstborn\u2019s brood, has thematic similarities, but is incredibly far removed from the incredibly mighty totem, that wouldn\u2019t create too many (or any) tensions for the character. Red Wolf (for example) isn\u2019t going to notice (or care) if a Uratha has \u2018Snow Runner - a wolf spirit that hunts through cold places\u2019 as a personal totem, even if it does have distant ties to Skolis-Ur. <br /> <br /> But if you mean a member of the Firstborn\u2019s personal brood, who has direct communion with the Firstborn and brings messages and direction to the werewolf, there\u2019s going to be quite a bit of tension for the character. In this case, Sagrim-Ur is going to be displeased with Snow Runner\u2019s meddling, and may come up with creative ways to complicate the werewolf\u2019s life - ranging from sending messengers to give instructions to the werewolf that are not in the personal totem\u2019s interests, to placing the werewolf in situations where she has to choose between breaking her tribal ban, or violating the personal totem\u2019s ban, to expressing its displeasure to the rest of the tribe so she suffers considerable social misery.<br /> <br /> You might question why Red Wolf would even notice or care about one werewolf at all, but again it comes down to spirits being slaves to their natures. The werewolf is part of that Firstborn\u2019s territory, and the two strongest urges Father Wolf gave to his children - werewolf or spirit - were territory and the hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}